msgid ""
"To run the latest ``devel`` branch without a checkout, create an isolated "
"Python environment, make sure ``pip``, ``setuptools`` and ``wheel`` are up "
"to date, and then:"
msgstr ""
"Para ejecutar la última rama ``devel`` sin un checkout, cree un entorno de "
"Python aislado, asegúrese de que ``pip``, ``setuptools`` y ``wheel`` están "
"al día y después:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:156
msgid ""
"That is the whole thing. It used to be two commands naming two "
"subdirectories, in the right order, because the repository shipped several "
"packages that pinned each other; it ships one now."
msgstr ""
"Eso es todo. Antes eran dos comandos que nombraban dos subdirectorios, en el"
" orden correcto, porque el repositorio distribuía varios paquetes que se "
"fijaban mutuamente; ahora distribuye uno."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:159
msgid ""
"For a checkout you intend to change, set the environment up as described "
"below instead -- an editable install is what makes ``pc`` run the code you "
"are editing."
msgstr ""
"Para un checkout que vaya a modificar, configure en su lugar el entorno como"
" se describe más abajo -- una instalación editable es lo que hace que ``pc``"
" ejecute el código que usted está editando."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:165
msgid "Environment"
msgstr "Entorno"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:167
msgid ""
"Our team is using `Visual Studio Code`_ and `Docker`_ which boosts software "
"development by providing a powerful, customizable editor and ensuring "
"consistent environments with containerization."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro equipo usa `Visual Studio Code`_ y `Docker`_, lo que impulsa el "
"desarrollo de software al proporcionar un editor potente y personalizable y "
"garantizar entornos consistentes mediante la contenerización."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:171
msgid ""
"VS Code's rich extensions and debugging tools integrate seamlessly with "
"Docker, allowing developers to write, test, and debug code within "
"containers."
msgstr ""
"Las ricas extensiones y herramientas de depuración de VS Code se integran "
"perfectamente con Docker, permitiendo a los desarrolladores escribir, probar"
" y depurar código dentro de contenedores."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:174
msgid ""
"This setup eliminates environment inconsistencies, accelerates development, "
"and improves team collaboration."
msgstr ""
"Esta configuración elimina las inconsistencias de entorno, acelera el "
"desarrollo y mejora la colaboración en equipo."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:177
msgid "Docker"
msgstr "Docker"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:179
msgid ""
"`Docker`_ helps build, share, run, and verify applications anywhere — "
"without tedious environment configuration or management. There are two main "
"options how to setup Docker."
msgstr ""
"`Docker`_ ayuda a construir, compartir, ejecutar y verificar aplicaciones en"
" cualquier lugar — sin tediosas configuraciones o gestión de entornos. Hay "
"dos opciones principales para configurar Docker."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:182
msgid ""
"If you do not have previous experience with Docker, then here is good place "
"to start:"
msgstr ""
"Si no tiene experiencia previa con Docker, este es un buen lugar para "
"empezar:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:184
msgid "`Docker Docs - Get Started`_"
msgstr "`Docker Docs - Get Started`_"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:187
msgid "Engine"
msgstr "Engine"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:189
msgid ""
"If your primary development system is Linux then you can install Docker "
"daemon directly on your host, see `Install`_ for more details on how to "
"install it in the distribution you're using. Minimum required versions:"
msgstr ""
"Si su sistema de desarrollo principal es Linux, puede instalar el daemon de "
"Docker directamente en su host; consulte `Install`_ para más detalles sobre "
"cómo instalarlo en la distribución que esté usando. Versiones mínimas "
"requeridas:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:192
msgid "Docker Engine: v27.4.0 or higher"
msgstr "Docker Engine: v27.4.0 o superior"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:193
msgid "Docker Desktop for Mac/Windows: 4.37.1 or higher"
msgstr "Docker Desktop para Mac/Windows: 4.37.1 o superior"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:197
msgid ""
"*`Docker Engine`_ is an open source containerization technology for building"
" and containerizing your applications. Docker Engine acts as a client-server"
" application with:*"
msgstr ""
"*`Docker Engine`_ es una tecnología de contenerización de código abierto "
"para construir y contenerizar sus aplicaciones. Docker Engine actúa como una"
" aplicación cliente-servidor con:*"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:200
msgid "A server with a long-running daemon process `dockerd`_."
msgstr "Un servidor con un proceso daemon de larga duración `dockerd`_."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:201
msgid ""
"APIs which specify interfaces that programs can use to talk to and instruct "
"the Docker daemon."
msgstr ""
"APIs que especifican interfaces que los programas pueden usar para "
"comunicarse con el daemon de Docker e instruirlo."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:202
msgid "A command line interface (CLI) client `Docker`_."
msgstr "Un cliente de interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI) `Docker`_."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:204
msgid ""
"The CLI uses `Docker APIs`_ to control or interact with the Docker daemon "
"through scripting or direct CLI commands. Many other Docker applications use"
" the underlying API and CLI. The daemon creates and manages Docker objects, "
"such as images, containers, networks, and volumes."
msgstr ""
"La CLI usa `Docker APIs`_ para controlar o interactuar con el daemon de "
"Docker mediante scripting o comandos directos de la CLI. Muchas otras "
"aplicaciones de Docker usan la API y la CLI subyacentes. El daemon crea y "
"gestiona objetos de Docker, como imágenes, contenedores, redes y volúmenes."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:208
msgid "For more details, see `Docker Architecture`_."
msgstr "Para más detalles, consulte `Docker Architecture`_."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:211
msgid "Desktop"
msgstr "Desktop"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:213
msgid ""
"If you're working on macOS or Windows, you can still install Engine, but "
"that would require managing a local Linux VM. Docker Desktop provides a "
"convenient solution and handles the required virtualization for you:"
msgstr ""
"Si trabaja en macOS o Windows, todavía puede instalar Engine, pero eso "
"requeriría gestionar una VM local de Linux. Docker Desktop proporciona una "
"solución conveniente y gestiona la virtualización requerida por usted:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:216
msgid "`Install on Mac`_"
msgstr "`Install on Mac`_"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:217
msgid "`Install on Windows`_"
msgstr "`Install on Windows`_"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:221
msgid ""
"*`Docker Desktop` is a one-click-install application for your Mac, Linux, or"
" Windows environment that lets you build, share, and run containerized "
"applications and microservices.*"
msgstr ""
"*`Docker Desktop` es una aplicación de instalación con un solo clic para su "
"entorno Mac, Linux o Windows que le permite construir, compartir y ejecutar "
"aplicaciones y microservicios contenerizados.*"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:224
msgid ""
"A screenshot of Docker Desktop's user interface, showing the \"Containers\" "
"tab."
msgstr ""
"Una captura de pantalla de la interfaz de usuario de Docker Desktop, "
"mostrando la pestaña \"Containers\"."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:230
msgid "Visual Studio Code"
msgstr "Visual Studio Code"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:232
msgid ""
"VS Code available for macOS, Linux, and Windows, has extensible architecture"
" and has rich customization and integration options. Here is good place to "
"get familiar with it:"
msgstr ""
"VS Code, disponible para macOS, Linux y Windows, tiene una arquitectura "
"extensible y ricas opciones de personalización e integración. Este es un "
"buen lugar para familiarizarse con él:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:235
msgid "`Setting up Visual Studio Code`_"
msgstr "`Setting up Visual Studio Code`_"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:239
msgid ""
"*Visual Studio Code combines the simplicity of a source code editor with "
"powerful developer tooling, like IntelliSense code completion and "
"debugging.*"
msgstr ""
"*Visual Studio Code combina la simplicidad de un editor de código fuente con"
" potentes herramientas de desarrollo, como el autocompletado de código "
"IntelliSense y la depuración.*"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:242
msgid ""
"*First and foremost, it is an editor that gets out of your way. The "
"delightfully frictionless edit-build-debug cycle means less time fiddling "
"with your environment, and more time executing on your ideas.*"
msgstr ""
"*Ante todo, es un editor que no se interpone en su camino. El ciclo de "
"edición-compilación-depuración, agradablemente sin fricciones, significa "
"menos tiempo dedicado a ajustar su entorno, y más tiempo ejecutando sus "
"ideas.*"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:245
msgid ""
"A screenshot of a Visual Studio Code environment. The terminal window shows "
"a behave command being executed to test BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) "
"scenarios for a PartCAD project."
msgstr ""
"Una captura de pantalla de un entorno de Visual Studio Code. La ventana de "
"terminal muestra un comando behave siendo ejecutado para probar escenarios "
"BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) de un proyecto de PartCAD."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:251
msgid "Dev Containers"
msgstr "Dev Containers"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:253
msgid ""
"VS Code also provides seamless integration with Docker for managing "
"environments by supporting `Dev Containers`_ specification."
msgstr ""
"VS Code también proporciona una integración perfecta con Docker para "
"gestionar entornos mediante el soporte de la especificación `Dev "
"Containers`_."

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:258
msgid ""
"_The Visual Studio Code Dev Containers extension lets you use a container as"
" a full-featured development environment. It allows you to open any folder "
"inside (or mounted into) a container and take advantage of Visual Studio "
"Code's full feature set. A `devcontainer.json`_ file in your project tells "
"VS Code how to access (or create) a development container with a well-"
"defined tool and runtime stack. This container can be used to run an "
"application or to separate tools, libraries, or runtimes needed for working "
"with a codebase._"
msgstr ""
"_La extensión Dev Containers de Visual Studio Code le permite usar un "
"contenedor como un entorno de desarrollo completo. Le permite abrir "
"cualquier carpeta dentro de (o montada en) un contenedor y aprovechar todo "
"el conjunto de funcionalidades de Visual Studio Code. Un archivo "
"`devcontainer.json`_ en su proyecto le indica a VS Code cómo acceder a (o "
"crear) un contenedor de desarrollo con un conjunto bien definido de "
"herramientas y tiempo de ejecución. Este contenedor se puede usar para "
"ejecutar una aplicación o para separar herramientas, bibliotecas o tiempos "
"de ejecución necesarios para trabajar con una base de código._"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:264
msgid "Following docs section provides good overview of available features:"
msgstr ""
"La siguiente sección de la documentación ofrece una buena visión general de "
"las funcionalidades disponibles:"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:266
msgid "`Developing inside a Container`_"
msgstr "`Developing inside a Container`_"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:284
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr "Inicio rápido"

#: ../../source/contributing.rst:288
msgid ""
"Following tutorial assumes that you have previous experience with both "
"`Visual Studio Code`_ and `Docker`_ or have read `Environment`_ first."
